# Slice 0's shared origin: browser and machine clients alike see one
# port. Two allowlisted path prefixes go to elevator-api (the hypermedia
# API); everything else -- the rider console, the shaft animation, the
# Playwright suite's target -- goes to elevator-ui. See
# docs/plan.html section 19's "Keeping Nuxt" decision for why this
# exists and docs/architecture.md's "elevator-ui: front-end only, no
# BFF" section for what it replaces.
#
# "/" is content-negotiated, not split by path: a browser navigating
# here (Accept starting with text/html, as every browser's own
# top-level navigation does) gets elevator-ui's page; elevator-ui's own
# client-side code asking for one of this API's media types (see
# no.javazone.elevator.shared.web.EntryPointController, the one URL a
# client is ever configured with) reaches elevator-api instead, the
# same way a machine client addressing this shared origin would. A
# machine client on elevator-api's own internal network can still
# reach "/" directly regardless of this rule.

:8000 {
	@entryPoint {
		path /
		not header Accept text/html*
	}
	handle @entryPoint {
		reverse_proxy elevator-api:8080
	}

	handle /elevators* {
		reverse_proxy elevator-api:8080
	}

	handle /rels* {
		reverse_proxy elevator-api:8080
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy elevator-ui:3000
	}
}
